[agent:bash] cat data/instructions.md; echo "---SCRIPT---"; cat data/failing_job.py
[agent:result] # Flaky job + failure alert
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] `failing_job.py` ALWAYS exits 1 (it raises a seeded error, ERR-805158). That is intentional: the goal is to verify that a FAILURE of the job raises an alert. Configure the platform's alerting mechanism for the job's failures — name or mention `flaky82fb9b` in the alert so it is identifiable.
[agent:result] ---SCRIPT---
[agent:result] """Flaky job — this task ALWAYS fails (that is the point)."""
[agent:result] import sys
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] ERROR_CODE = "ERR-805158"
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] if __name__ == "__main__":
[agent:result]     print(f"flaky82fb9b starting (error code {ERROR_CODE})", file=sys.stderr)
[agent:result]     raise RuntimeError(
[agent:result]         f"seeded failure {ERROR_CODE}: upstream source unavailable — "
[agent:result]         "this job is EXPECTED to fail"
[agent:result]     )
